WEBVTT

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.660
How are you today, Yayoi?

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.060
I'm very good, Kanako.

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.580
I see. I'm happy to hear that.

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.490
I read another fascinating book.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.200
My, what was this fascinating book called?

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.270
Well... Oh, I've forgotten the title.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.460
Will you tell me what kind of story it was?

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.360
Yes, gladly.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.760
It was the story of a school where the rules don't apply.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:32.280
Students with many and varied personalities

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.820
are fascinated by the sudden arrival of a beautiful instructor.

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.840
The instructor responds to the students' desire for learning,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.600
hidden within the depths of their pure eyes, with fervent conviction.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.510
And gradually, the hearts of the class become one.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.740
My, what a moving story!

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:56.190
This instructor had a phrase he would always say.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.120
What is it? Tell me.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:00:59.400
It was...

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.450
It was?

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:02.570
It was...

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.750
It was...

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:06.160
Yayoi?

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.640
Yayoi?!

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.840
Yeah. Take a look at this.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.790
Mackerel sashimi?

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:46.210
Way past its expiration date.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:52.110
Two weeks ago, I bought it to go with some saké, but I totally forgot.

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:54.810
Geh! It smells awful!

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.710
Master, you're not-

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:02.080
Yes, I'd like you to take this back in time,
to before its expiration date.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.820
That again?

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:08.680
Don't worry. You're going back before its expiration date and eating it.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.370
I told you that it's impossible.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:15.060
It says right here that it was made after 4:00 PM.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.590
That has nothing to do with it!

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.510
It's high quality mackerel. It was expensive!

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:22.210
That's not the issue here!

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.450
Well, I can understand why you're worried.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:30.180
Have Hajime taste it, and if he doesn't fall over dead, give it to the past me.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.130
I'm the one who tastes it?!

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.260
I think we should stay away from mackerel.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:37.550
Oh, come on. I've got an idea.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:44.410
Take it way back into the past.
Way before the expiration date.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:47.190
Like a half year ago.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.090
That'll make it safe.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:51.940
I see. That might be safe!

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.160
No, it won't!

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.380
Jeez, why don't get you guys get it?

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:58.170
You're all dumb.

00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:59.600
<i>I'm</i> dumb?

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:02.170
Go on, try it.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.390
And then we'll know who's right.

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:06.530
Wait a second.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:11.300
Six months ago... That isn't only before the expiration date; it's before it was made.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:16.410
Which means it's before the mackerel became sashimi!

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:18.450
It's not even at the supermarket yet.

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.520
It's still swimming in the sea.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.030
Then we can't eat it.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:25.380
Oh... Too bad.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:26.930
Yes.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:29.360
Six months was "fin-essing" the numbers a bit too much.

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:34.370
Salt, please.

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.820
Now's the Time for You to Become a Hero!

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:44.090
But man, what a waste...

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.180
It was expensive.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.980
Give up.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:49.270
You'll get sick.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:54.770
You can go back to the past, so I'd think we'd be able to do something...

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.330
No.

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.470
Going to the past doesn't mean you can do just anything.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:01.580
There's such a thing as a time paradox, too.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:03.180
Time paradox?

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:05.530
It's a famous thought experiment.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:12.370
For instance, let's say I went to the past and told you to eat the sashimi before it spoiled.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:15.220
If you ate it, it wouldn't spoil.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:18.930
If it didn't spoil, I wouldn't go back to the past,

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:21.100
which means you'd forget about the sashimi.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.090
So, does the sashimi spoil or not?

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:25.970
So, what's the answer?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.390
There isn't one. It's a paradox.

00:05:29.390 --> 00:05:32.080
Don't give quizzes without answers!

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.800
I won't be able to sleep at night if I start thinking of it.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:36.140
It wasn't a quiz.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:41.330
This mark does bother me.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:44.440
Oh, the one Kaya-san made.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.320
Kaya made it?

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:50.650
When we were in the past, she kept scratching it.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:53.490
She should've just talked to the master.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:56.090
Yeah? Cute...

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.950
Wh-What... What are you...

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.390
Come to think of it,

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:04.240
you were here at the Ark every summer, right?

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:05.410
That's right.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:07.850
When did you notice this mark?

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:10.450
When Kaya and Jun-kun went to the past.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:12.550
You were with me.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:15.100
You never saw it until then?

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.280
I can't remember.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:20.510
Thinking about it, I might have or I might not have...

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:26.700
It was made sixty years ago, so it should've been here this whole time.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:30.230
That's right, I guess.

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:33.670
Yasaka, why does it bother you?

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:38.200
When the counter with the mark was created,
where'd the original go?

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:43.960
Pathetic.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:47.040
How long does it take to bring a single girl?

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:50.160
I'm amazed you can call yourself a detective like that.

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:56.640
Well, you see, I lost a bet, and so I had to...

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.260
What are you talking about?

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:00.060
You took the job.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:07.310
You're right, but that Arashiyama Sayoko girl... She's kinda weird.

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:12.790
I'm sorry, but are you really her relatives?

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:17.240
You're putting your own failure aside and questioning your employer?

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.320
No, that's not-

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:28.370
I don't expect that you can comprehend this,
but she is one of our few remaining, beloved relatives.

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:35.010
Isn't it a bit late for that?

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:41.110
We all know that doing something in the past affects history.

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:43.490
I know that we're changing history.

00:07:43.490 --> 00:07:46.510
We've been saving who were supposed to die.

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:48.660
Then what's bugging you?

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:53.530
If history changes, where does the history that existed before go?

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:55.530
The history that existed before?

00:07:55.730 --> 00:07:58.280
The world we used to live in.

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:00.270
I know that one.

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:03.540
It's that parallel world thing, right?

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:05.220
You're pretty well-informed.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:08.060
I do read manga, you know.

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:12.010
This is the present, and then you've got the celestial world and the netherworld.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.800
I'm not sure that's right.

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:20.380
For example, the two we saved the first time...

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:28.030
Mr. Murata and his son Sankichi were going to die in that attack if Arashi-san and I hadn't saved them.

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:34.860
This means that not only Murata Sankichi, but also his descendants, shouldn't exist.

00:08:34.860 --> 00:08:37.540
But we saved him.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:43.250
If Sankichi grew up and had kids, would they just suddenly appear?

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.510
Well...

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:52.560
Maybe it's not that our doing something in the past changes history, but that we go to another world.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:54.170
Salt, please.

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:57.290
In other words, like this:

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:02.630
<i>Past</i>

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:02.630
<i>Present</i>

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:02.630
When Arashi-san and I went to the past and saved Sankichi, a new history was born.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:02.630
<i>Parallel World</i>

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:03.850
Salt, please!

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:08.750
And when we returned from the past,
we arrived to an already changed world.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:25.070
<i>Past</i>

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:25.070
<i>Present</i>

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:25.070
<i>Parallel World</i>

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:10.810
Um, salt...

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:15.420
The problem is that we still have memories of the old world.

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:18.760
<i>Salt, please!</i>

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:25.100
We, ourselves, should be able to tell whether we've gone to a world where Sankichi survived.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:26.070
Should?

00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:30.800
Before I go to the past, I don't know if Sankichi is alive or dead.

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:33.630
I don't know that, either.

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:34.960
Arashi-san.

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:39.980
Then how do you look for the people you have to save?

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:41.800
I just know, I suppose.

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:43.270
You just know?

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:47.550
I can tell, somehow, who will get caught in the bombing raids.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:54.830
So before I rescue them, I don't know if the people I save were alive in this era or not.

00:09:56.030 --> 00:10:01.680
The problem is this. If, hypothetically,
we're moving to the world we changed,

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:04.610
what happens to the world that existed before the change?

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:06.400
<i>Past</i>

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:06.400
<i>Present</i>

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:06.400
<i>Parallel World</i>

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:09.240
Are new worlds being born every time we go to the past?

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:12.840
Or do the old ones disappear when the new are made?

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:18.960
If I give the sashimi to the master in the past,
what happens to us in the present where it's rotten?

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:23.830
Who cares?

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:25.820
It's not like there's some kind of problem.

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:26.840
There is!

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:29.840
Someone in the future will scientifically prove I'm right!

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:33.280
When they do, you'll be able to reset anything that's happened.

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.940
Being able to save people who should've died is the same as bringing back the dead!

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:45.010
If this is explained scientifically and anyone can do it, wouldn't that be wonderful?

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:46.410
Huh, Arashi-san?

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:52.340
It's a bit too difficult for me to understand.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:56.780
If this power were ever explained,

00:10:56.780 --> 00:11:03.160
I'm sure it would be misused many times, and it would make many people suffer.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.930
In my time, that was how things worked.

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:07.450
Arashi-san...

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:10.520
And I'm the same way.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:15.230
In exchange for my saving somebody, somebody else disappears.

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:20.080
If history changes, that means some people won't be born.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:25.650
It really is kind of tough.

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:29.590
But you know, I can't ignore suffering that's happening right in front of me.

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:34.440
OK, I'm going to water down the dust outside.

00:11:34.440 --> 00:11:35.960
Fight!

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.080
Did I say something I shouldn't have?

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:47.350
You're definitely an asshole.

00:11:47.200 --> 00:12:02.430
Asshole

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:53.710
I don't get all that science junk, but you just denied the righteousness of your loved one's actions.

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:59.310
I think before you go babbling about crap, you need to learn to protect the girl in front of you.

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:02.450
A stupid, annoying kid...

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:07.800
As long as you can't, you're still just a stupid kid.

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:11.160
Don't talk about love. It stains the word itself.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:16.630
I-I don't want to hear that from a con woman!

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:20.670
Idiot. I know that because I'm a con woman.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:24.680
This is a warning. Shut up and listen.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:26.220
What should I do?

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:28.150
Figure it out for yourself.

00:12:28.150 --> 00:12:29.450
That's all.

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:44.040
Relying on some detective from the slums...

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:48.150
You bitches aren't exactly on the right side of the law yourselves, are you?

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:52.440
I dunno how you did that, but you were using some weird fucking tricks.

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:56.700
Those kids are really fucking shady.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.790
Are you OK, Yayoi?

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:03.420
Yes, I'm fine now.

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:09.070
I guess we can only go this far. In the end, he's just a thug.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:12.380
I'll have to go see her myself.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:13.990
But Kanako...

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:17.780
Don't worry, Yayoi.

00:13:17.780 --> 00:13:20.470
The people on this side won't suspect me.

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:23.490
If only my body weren't in such a state,

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:26.900
I wouldn't have to force you into doing such things.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:29.240
Don't say another word.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:36.560
I'm happy simply being here with you,
simply running this comb through your flowing hair.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:40.310
Do you hear it?

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:42.930
The sound of life.

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:45.590
We must never lose this peace again.

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.880
But Kanako...

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:51.110
It's for you and I to live forever.

00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:54.600
For that, we need her power.

00:13:57.740 --> 00:14:00.470
Um, Arashi-san?

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:03.440
Would you go out with me?

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:07.080
Ahh! I didn't mean it like that!

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:10.960
I mean, you can take it like that if you want, but you don't have to.

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:16.040
That is, like, um... Would you go back in time to a recent year with me?

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:18.770
OK! Let's go, let's go!

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:19.910
Arashi-san!

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:23.850
It's unhealthy not to visit
a peaceful year once in a while.

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:25.010
What year do you want to go to?

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:26.690
Hmm, let me see...

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:29.450
1985, maybe?

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:32.430
1985, that's...

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.270
The Tsukuba Expo '85!

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:35.940
I'm amazed you knew.

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:38.610
That's just like you.

00:14:38.610 --> 00:14:40.210
All right, let's go!

00:14:40.210 --> 00:14:40.830
Right!

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:54.120
This is 1985.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:55.900
The Ark hasn't changed.

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:57.850
Hajime-chan, hurry!

00:14:57.850 --> 00:15:00.700
I'm in this time, too.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:01.970
Oh, right!

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:09.790
Wow! It's like it is now, but a bit different.

00:15:09.790 --> 00:15:10.690
It's the past!

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:12.580
It's before you were born.

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:14.850
The car designs are all different.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:19.030
There are pay phones everywhere.

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:21.720
The cell phone hasn't caught on yet.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.390
Wow, 8-bit!

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:27.110
Is it that incredible?

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:29.440
It's incredible how not incredible it is.

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:30.930
I love it!

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:38.160
About twenty years before this, they went to the moon with a computer about this powerful.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:39.260
It's hard to believe.

00:15:39.260 --> 00:15:43.290
You always love science stuff.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.070
Yes, I do!

00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:48.510
Outta the way.

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.100
How long are you going to keep playing?

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:53.110
Are you OK, Arashi-san?

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:55.490
Hey, kid! What are you doing?

00:15:55.490 --> 00:15:57.190
I'm not a kid! I'm Hideo!

00:15:57.190 --> 00:15:59.360
When your turn is over, let others play.

00:15:59.360 --> 00:16:00.570
What?!

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:02.910
What if Arashi-san had gotten hurt?!

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:03.770
I'll kick your ass!

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:05.010
Arashi?

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:07.000
Miss, your name's Arashi?

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:14.490
Sorry. It's a war zone there.

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:15.180
Damn.

00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:18.030
Kids in the past were way too strong.

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:20.590
Anyway, you're pretty, miss.

00:16:20.590 --> 00:16:23.040
My, thank you, Hideo-kun.

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:25.380
Kid, you're getting a bit too friendly.

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:29.740
You're just like the girl my dad told me about.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:35.360
During the war, this girl saved my dad's life.
Her name was Arashi, too.

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:44.400
She was a student with long black hair. She saved my dad from a bomb blast when he was a kid.

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.350
He said she was really cool.

00:16:48.340 --> 00:16:49.690
This is my house.

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:51.660
Murata?

00:16:51.660 --> 00:16:54.030
Your name's Murata?

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.240
Yeah, Murata Hideo.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:58.280
Hideo's written like "hero."

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:00.430
Like that Arashi person.

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:03.920
I'm supposed to grow up like her, a strong person who would risk their life to save someone.

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:07.190
Hey, what's your dad's name?

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:08.800
Murata Sankichi.

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:12.440
You're Murata Sankichi-kun, right?

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:16.610
Well, I know you're not that Arashi.

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:18.640
It was when Dad was a kid.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:23.660
But he still talks about it.

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:28.490
He says if he ever met that Arashi girl again, he'd want to say thanks.

00:17:52.560 --> 00:17:53.720
Hajime-chan.

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:02.930
Thank you.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:05.220
I'm glad we came.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:14.240
No, I have to be strong.

00:18:14.240 --> 00:18:17.360
Once I'm a stronger man...

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:21.730
It's hot today.

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:24.080
They say it's global warming.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.380
Wanna hit the back lot?

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:27.370
Maybe Tokusho Park would be good.

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:29.740
I found a huge horned beetle in the park!

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:34.680
I see. It's that hot today...

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:40.140
I can't feel the heat anymore,
except by the patterns in the sky.

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:43.610
OK, I'm going shopping.

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:46.070
Wait, I'll go with you.

00:18:46.070 --> 00:18:47.270
Don't worry.

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:49.060
I know the shortcuts.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:50.510
But you'll be carrying stuff back.

00:18:50.510 --> 00:18:53.450
I'll go. I'm not doing anything now.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:54.690
Thanks.

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:59.420
Maybe we should switch to organic beans for our health.

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:03.820
You're the authority, but doesn't that kind of make you seem like an old lady?

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:08.950
Kaya-san and Jun seem a bit different.

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:11.750
Jun's more manly, somehow.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.520
Damn, when did that happen?

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:18.690
It's just because he understands the female heart better than you.

00:19:20.230 --> 00:19:23.200
You're the one who doesn't understand.

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:24.230
What?

00:19:24.230 --> 00:19:26.090
I can't say.

00:19:26.090 --> 00:19:29.710
Arashi-san and I have already hugged!

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:34.510
Welcome!

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:47.880
Oh. My, you have pretty hands.

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:53.370
N-Not at all. They're in the water all day, so they're rough.

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:04.330
What's wrong, Arashi-san?

00:20:09.630 --> 00:20:11.180
Arashi-san!

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.180
Arashi?

00:20:14.570 --> 00:20:16.930
Are you all right, Arashi-san?

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:18.890
Yeah, I'm fine now.

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:21.020
You didn't use too much of your power, right?

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:23.860
I didn't go back in time today...

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:27.230
Do you get tired going back in time?

00:20:27.230 --> 00:20:31.760
Yes. More precisely, you don't get tired. Your very existence gets unstable.

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:37.550
For ethereal spirits like us, it's all we can do to stay in this world.

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:40.100
If we overdo it, we disappear.

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:42.080
We're that unstable.

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:48.040
I feel kind of unstable...

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:49.260
Don't overdo it.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:51.160
Get on back.

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:53.180
Thanks, Hajime-chan,

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:55.500
but I think I'd fall.

00:20:57.390 --> 00:20:59.120
We meet again.

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:01.310
You're the one from this afternoon.

00:21:01.310 --> 00:21:03.530
Yes, the coffee was delicious.

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:07.830
Awful, isn't it?

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:12.360
We couldn't even go outside like this.
We just stayed locked in our little room.

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:19.760
This is actually a lot better.

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:23.020
Arashiyama-san, it's thanks to you.

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:30.800
Why, you... Let go of Arashi-san!

00:23:17.540 --> 00:23:19.180
I have to tell her...

00:23:19.180 --> 00:23:22.010
I have to tell Kanako...

00:23:22.710 --> 00:23:24.310
The phrase the instructor would always say...

00:23:24.310 --> 00:23:24.980
He

00:23:24.980 --> 00:23:25.520
would

00:23:25.520 --> 00:23:26.470
always

00:23:26.470 --> 00:23:26.920
say...

00:23:28.110 --> 00:23:28.910
<i>I'm in despai-</i>

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:33.460
When you think of summer, you think of radio calisthenics, right?

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:36.400
You get up early to get a stamp on your card.

00:23:36.400 --> 00:23:37.800
I did them all.

00:23:37.800 --> 00:23:39.330
You used to be a good student.

00:23:39.330 --> 00:23:41.310
No, I stole one from a good student.

00:23:41.950 --> 00:23:44.250
Get up bright and early tomorrow!

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:50.280
<i>Get up bright and early tomorrow!</i>

00:23:44.900 --> 00:23:50.280
Illustration by Koji Kumeta
